{
  "version": 1,
  "model": "monster.glb",
  "notes": [
    "three.js removes ':', '.', '/', '[', ']' from node names and turns spaces into '_' (PropertyBinding.sanitizeNodeName), so 'mixamorig:Head' becomes 'mixamorigHead'.",
    "Colour pipeline, in linear RGB: base colour -> fur hue/saturation/value where furMask is white -> face overlay mixed by its alpha -> mood saturation/value -> multiply by mood tint.",
    "Overlays and masks use the same UV set as the material's base colour texture; load them with flipY = false.",
    "Dirt is straight RGBA mud mixed over the fur colour, before the face overlay, by alpha times the mood's dirt amount.",
    "The children of the Flies node are flies built around their own origins, facing +Z: circle them around the Flies node's vertical axis."
  ],
  "materials": {
    "Body": {
      "uv": 0,
      "furMask": "textures/fur_mask_body.webp",
      "dirt": "textures/dirt_body.webp"
